  just a rehash of a bunch of moves that  we are already familiar with there are  lots of combat tools to engage with such  as the parry and claw so it makes for a  better one-on-one than say eldon rings  mimic boss fight but it pales in  comparison to something like ishin and  sekiro where we get that kind of duel  between equals but still have a wide  variety of new moves and attacks that  add to the fight's engagement factor and  its spectacle maybe it would have been  better to have corvus be a phase one and  then grow to something more unique in  phase two like turn more crow than human  undergo a dark sinister transformation  that could fit with the corrupting and  empowering blood motifs that are present  in the lore and we do see something  similar to that with one of the earlier  bosses it's just that the game separates  it into two different fights the game  could in general have more amped up  phase 2s for bosses that would help with  the difficulty and this fight especially  could use the buff to make it something  a lot more distinct and memorable it  could even have been a better fight if  boss corvus could use perry so you can't  just spam attack at him during any  opening having a little bit of this  would keep the player a bit more on edge  and it would feel better and more  natural since we have a parry and we're  supposed to be fighting ourself but boss  corvus never parries us  overall thymesia shines during some of  the boss fights but the lack of  development in most other areas  especially enemy variety holds it back i  had fun with the game i enjoyed a bit of  the exploration and the fights but i  didn't get much more of a cohesive  experience other than those few moments  where the dance of combat really clicked  and one final note i forgot to mention  earlier the soundtrack to the game is  fine the main theme is fitting and  grandiose in the right way but most of  the others are somewhat forgettable to  me i will say that the os stage to the  first level did have an adequately fun  yet kind of creepy investigative vibe so  the main theme and level one ost are  solid the rest were so soft and that  concludes most of what i have to say  about thymeja in terms of a critical  review it has its positives but the lack  of development shows in a lot of areas i  may do one or two more videos on the  game such as an endings guide an  explanation or maybe something about the  lore or bosses so if you like this video  wants to see that content or want to see  more of my usual elden ring content feel  free to subscribe to the channel or  become a patron on patreon both really  help the channel out and let me dedicate  more time and effort into making these  videos with that thank you for watching  i hope you enjoyed and i will see you in  the next video peace  [Music]
 

